<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Dynamic_waypoints">Dynamic waypoints</span></h2>
<p>Is it possible to create waypoints dynamically with CreateObject? If so, what is the resource name required by the function? --<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20Valgreon" title="User:Valgreon (page does not exist)">Valgreon</a> 17:15, 7 February 2010 (UTC)
</p>
<ul><li><a rel="nofollow" class="external free" href="http://social.bioware.com/wiki/datoolset/index.php/OBJECT_TYPE*">http://social.bioware.com/wiki/datoolset/index.php/OBJECT_TYPE*</a> <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20Eshme" title="User:Eshme (page does not exist)">Eshme</a> 08:12, 8 February 2010 (UTC)</li></ul>
<dl><dd><dl><dd> The <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/CreateObject" title="CreateObject">CreateObject</a> function requires a resource template as one of its parameters, but waypoints don't have resources. I wouldn't know how to work around that limitation offhand, has anyone managed to create waypoints dynamically that way (or any other way for that matter)? There's a feature request for this ability at <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Feature%20Request%20-%20CreateWaypoint%20script%20function" title="Feature Request: CreateWaypoint script function">Feature Request: CreateWaypoint script function</a> but if someone figures out a workaround we could use our programming resources to work on something else instead.&#160;:) <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20BryanDerksen" title="User:BryanDerksen">BryanDerksen</a> 23:13, 8 February 2010 (UTC)</dd></dl></dd></dl>
